 ### Commitment rule
-A coordinator may mark the entry at index N committed (set `commitIndex` to N, for N greater than its current `commitIndex`) only if (a) the entry at N carries the coordinator's **current** epoch, and (b) a majority of the coordinator's configuration (counting the coordinator if it is a member) have `matchIndex ≥ N`. Committing N commits every earlier entry. Entries from earlier epochs are therefore committed only indirectly, when a later entry of the current epoch is committed.
